IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vic-nouns`
IMPORT `vic-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `vic-part4-a-aids`
IMPORT `vic-part4-b-powers`
IMPORT `vic-part4-c-general`
IMPORT `vic-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer: a person with a time limit to meet under a Victorian Act or statutory rule.
-- Each expected value is written by hand from the section named beside it, using calendar facts checked for the days named:
-- 16 July 2028 is a Sunday, 1 September 2030 is a Sunday, 31 January 2026 is a Saturday, 2 February 2026 is a Monday.

§ `When does my period end, and which of my days count? (s 44)`

-- Thirty days from 1 January 2026 (s 44(1): 1 January is left out): the thirtieth day after it is 31 January 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 VicDays TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- Five years from 15 January 2025: both readings of s 44(1) and (6)(b),(c) give 15 January 2030.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 15 1 2025) 5 VicYears TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
-- Five years from 1 September 2025: both readings give 1 September 2030.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 9 2025) 5 VicYears TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2030)
-- Three years from 16 July 2025: both readings give 16 July 2028.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 16 7 2025) 3 VicYears TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 16 7 2028)
-- One month from 15 January 2025: 15 February 2025.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 15 1 2025) 1 VicCalendarMonths TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 15 2 2025)
-- Two months from 31 December 2025, one month from 31 January 2024 and one year from 29 February 2024: the text does not say which day. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 31 12 2025) 2 VicCalendarMonths TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 31 1 2024) 1 VicCalendarMonths TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 29 2 2024) 1 VicYears TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A period of weeks: the text defines month and year but not week. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 1 2026) 2 VicWeeks TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A period "after" the day: s 44(1) speaks of a period that begins on or is reckoned from a day. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 VicDays FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 44(1), (2): the day of a "from" period is left out; the day of a "to" period is counted.
#ASSERT `Does the day I count from count in my period` VicReckonedFromDay EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the day I count from count in my period` VicBeginsOnDay EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the day I count from count in my period` VicReckonedToDay EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the day I count from count in my period` VicEndsOnDay EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the day I count from count in my period` VicAfterDay EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 44(3), (4): 16 July 2028 is a Sunday, so the time extends to Monday 17 July 2028; if that is a public holiday, to Tuesday 18 July 2028.
#ASSERT `By which day may I do the thing` (Date 16 7 2028) TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 17 7 2028)
#ASSERT `By which day may I do the thing` (Date 16 7 2028) TRUE (LIST Date 17 7 2028) EQUALS JUST (Date 18 7 2028)
-- Saturday 31 January 2026 extends to Monday 2 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By which day may I do the thing` (Date 31 1 2026) TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
-- Friday 30 January 2026 is not a Saturday, a Sunday or listed as a public holiday: the time is not extended.
#ASSERT `By which day may I do the thing` (Date 30 1 2026) TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 30 1 2026)
-- Friday 30 January 2026 listed as a public holiday: the next day that is not a holiday is Monday 2 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By which day may I do the thing` (Date 30 1 2026) TRUE (LIST Date 30 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
-- Not a time limited for doing something: s 44(3) does not speak to it. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `By which day may I do the thing` (Date 31 1 2026) FALSE EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

-- The two together: thirty days from 1 January 2026 ends on Saturday 31 January 2026; as a time limited for doing something it extends to Monday 2 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By which day must I do the thing` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 VicDays TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
-- With 2 February 2026 a public holiday: Tuesday 3 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By which day must I do the thing` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 VicDays TRUE TRUE (LIST Date 2 2 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 3 2 2026)
-- Not a time limited for doing something: the last day stays 31 January 2026.
#ASSERT `By which day must I do the thing` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 VicDays TRUE FALSE EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- Five years from 1 September 2025 ends on Sunday 1 September 2030; extended to Monday 2 September 2030.
#ASSERT `By which day must I do the thing` (Date 1 9 2025) 5 VicYears TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS JUST (Date 2 9 2030)
-- A period of weeks: the period's last day is not covered, so neither is the day it extends to.
#ASSERT `By which day must I do the thing` (Date 1 1 2026) 2 VicWeeks TRUE TRUE EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

§ `When does an Act, a provision or a rule take effect? (ss 10A, 11, 12, 24, 25)`

-- s 11(1), (2): a day fixed by the Act itself: the Act comes into operation at the beginning of that day.
#ASSERT `At which moment does the Act or provision come into operation` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS JUST (VicInOperationFrom (VicMoment OF (Date 1 3 2026), VicBeginningOfDay))
-- s 11(2): fixed by a proclamation published on or before the fixed day: the beginning of the fixed day.
#ASSERT `At which moment does the Act or provision come into operation` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 20 2 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST (VicInOperationFrom (VicMoment OF (Date 1 3 2026), VicBeginningOfDay))
-- s 11(2A): a proclamation made on or before the fixed day but published on 5 March 2026: the beginning of 5 March 2026.
#ASSERT `At which moment does the Act or provision come into operation` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 5 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST (VicInOperationFrom (VicMoment OF (Date 5 3 2026), VicBeginningOfDay))
-- s 11: a proclamation not yet published: not yet in operation.
#ASSERT `At which moment does the Act or provision come into operation` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE EQUALS JUST VicNotYetInOperation
-- A proclamation made after the fixed day and published after it: the text does not say. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `At which moment does the Act or provision come into operation` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 5 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 10A(3), (4): passed on 10 March 2026 with no commencement provision and nothing proclaimed: the first anniversary, 10 March 2027.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act that says nothing about its commencement come into operation` (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2027)
-- A day proclaimed earlier than the anniversary: that day. A day proclaimed later: the anniversary.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act that says nothing about its commencement come into operation` (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 6 2026)
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act that says nothing about its commencement come into operation` (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2027)
-- Passed on 29 February 2028: the text does not say which day is the first anniversary in a year without a 29 February. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act that says nothing about its commencement come into operation` (Date 29 2 2028) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 12, s 25: a temporary Act, provision or rule continues until the last moment of the day it is expressed to expire on.
#ASSERT `Until which moment does a temporary Act, provision or rule stay in operation` (Date 30 6 2027) FALSE EQUALS VicMoment OF (Date 30 6 2027), VicLastMomentOfDay
#ASSERT `Until which moment does a temporary Act, provision or rule stay in operation` (Date 30 6 2027) TRUE EQUALS VicMoment OF (Date 30 6 2027), VicLastMomentOfDay

§ `Service by post (s 49)`

-- s 49(1): properly addressed, prepaid and posted, with no contrary intention: taken to be served when the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course.
#ASSERT `On which day is a document I posted taken to have been served` VicOrdinaryPost TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 14 4 2026)
-- s 49(2): registered post or certified mail: the same.
#ASSERT `On which day is a document I posted taken to have been served` VicRegisteredPostOrCertifiedMail TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 15 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 15 4 2026)
-- Not prepaid, or a contrary intention, or the contrary proved: the text does not give a day. Not covered. Asserted.
#ASSERT `On which day is a document I posted taken to have been served` VicOrdinaryPost TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day is a document I posted taken to have been served` VicOrdinaryPost TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 14 4 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day is a document I posted taken to have been served` VicOrdinaryPost TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 4 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reading the Act or rule that sets my limit (ss 36, 42C, 45, 52, 53)`

-- s 36(2A): a heading to a section forms part of an Act passed on or after 1 January 2001, and not of one passed before it unless inserted by a later Act.
#ASSERT `Does the item printed with my Act form part of the Act` VicHeadingToASectionClauseRegulationRuleOrItem (Date 1 1 2001) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the item printed with my Act form part of the Act` VicHeadingToASectionClauseRegulationRuleOrItem (Date 31 12 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the item printed with my Act form part of the Act` VicHeadingToASectionClauseRegulationRuleOrItem (Date 31 12 2000) TRUE (Date 1 6 2005) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 36(3): a marginal note does not form part of the Act, whatever its date.
#ASSERT `Does the item printed with my Act form part of the Act` VicMarginalNote (Date 1 1 2010) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 42C(1)
#ASSERT `Is the decision about me ineffective only because the official was irregularly appointed` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the decision about me ineffective only because the official was irregularly appointed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 45(1), (2)
#ASSERT `Does the official have a choice whether to use the power` VicMay TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the official have a choice whether to use the power` VicShall TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the official have a choice whether to use the power` VicMay FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the official use the power` VicShall TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the official use the power` VicMay TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 52
#ASSERT `Must my matter be heard only by the Magistrates' Court` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my matter be heard only by the Magistrates' Court` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my matter be heard only by the Magistrates' Court` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my matter be heard only by the Magistrates' Court` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 53
#ASSERT `Is the form I used good enough` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the form I used good enough` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the form I used good enough` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
